# GT6 obtain: no catalog ItemEntity worldgen

Do not sprinkle catalog items onto the overworld as `ItemEntity` so a card
can claim empty-input survival obtain. That is how T33/T45/T48 remainder /
MTE / food / machine tags were faked. It is not GT6.

GT6 overworld scatter is **rock blocks** (`WorldgenRocks` →
`SurfaceRockFeature`), plus real trees, ores, dungeons, loot. Translate
those. Do not invent dirt/sand rarity dumps of tagged catalogs.

**Forbidden** (do not write this in a new/active plan, GameTest, or
`player_path_support`):

- `GtItemScatterFeature`, `GtStoneScatterFeature`,
  `GtBlockObjectScatterFeature`, `ItemScatterConfiguration`, new `*_scatter`
  holders, or biome modifiers that spawn `ItemEntity` or dump a catalog
  onto dirt/sand during chunk gen
- Re-registering any of the eight retired fake scatters
- 「empty-input overworld item scatter」or「用主世界掉落物顶 player_complete」
- Recording `kind: worldgen_drop` of a remainder catalog as obtain

Creative tabs and GameTest inject are still not acquisition. If GT6 has no
recipe and no real worldgen: keep `runtime_ready` / `blocked`. Live count of
those fake feature registrations must stay **0**.

Human contract: `docs/current/gt6-no-item-entity-worldgen.md`.
